# Whitelist build context for every image built from the repository root (api/worker delivery + dev targets,
# rag, ifc, node_gateway). Everything is excluded, then only what a Dockerfile COPYs is let back in: organizer data
# (case_data, learning_data, New_data), internal reports (*.md, evaluation/), agent memory (.claude), local
# databases, logs, venv and secrets can never reach an image or the build context. A new COPY needs a line here.
*

!api_service/requirements.txt
!api_service/app
!api_service/alembic
!api_service/alembic.ini
!evaluation/__init__.py
!evaluation/metrics.py
!evaluation/exporter.py
!evaluation/errors.py
!evaluation/candidate_coverage.py

# dev target / legacy services only (docker-compose.yml)
!shared
!rag_service/requirements.txt
!rag_service/app
!ifc_service/requirements.txt
!ifc_service/app
!node_gateway/package.json
!node_gateway/server.js
!node_gateway/openapi.json

**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite
**/*.log
